From fe0a97394265d100109324dd1fd35db553cab3a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicolai Stange <nstange@suse.de>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 05:54:12 +0200
References: jsc#PED-15986,bsc#1262160
Patch-mainline: Never, downstream workaround to meet certification requirements.
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: introduce downstream CRYPTO_ALG_FIPS_UNAPPROVED

In general, crypto algorithm implementations not approved by FIPS
have their ->fips flag clear in the associated testmgr entry and their
usage is prohibited altogether. So far, algorithms that are clearly
not intended for cryptographic use but are still getting made available
through the generic crypto API, use such as crc32 or compression
algorithms, had been tolerated to have ->fips == true.

This is about to change though -- e.g. it's been raised that xxhash64
cannot be considered an approved security function, the main concern
being that it has "hash" in its name, which might perhaps suggest to
some that it qualifies as a cryptographic hash.

xxhash64 must be remain usable in FIPS mode though, so its associated
->fips cannot get flipped to false.

So, implement a workaround roughly analogous to the already existing
downstream CRYPTO_TFM_FIPS_COMPLIANCE, which got introduced to handle
a similar situation (external IV generation for gcm(aes)).

Introduce the new downstream CRYPTO_ALG_FIPS_UNAPPROVED flag. It will
get set for certain algorithm implementations, such as xxhash64.
Supporting FIPS certification documents will include a note that this
flag must get checked for in a crypto_alg's ->cra_flags in order to
determine its approvedness. Note that no one will actually examine this
flag in practice, the mere capability to do so is sufficient to meet
the requirements. Add the new CRYPTO_ALG_FIPS_UNAPPROVED to
CRYPTO_ALG_INHERITED_FLAGS so that it contaminates relying crypto
template instantiations.

Signed-off-by: Nicolai Stange <nstange@suse.de>
---
 include/crypto/algapi.h |    2 +-
 include/linux/crypto.h  |   12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/include/crypto/algapi.h
+++ b/include/crypto/algapi.h
@@ -237,7 +237,7 @@ static inline u32 crypto_requires_off(st
  */
 #define CRYPTO_ALG_INHERITED_FLAGS	\
 	(CRYPTO_ALG_ASYNC | CRYPTO_ALG_NEED_FALLBACK |	\
-	 CRYPTO_ALG_ALLOCATES_MEMORY)
+	 CRYPTO_ALG_ALLOCATES_MEMORY | CRYPTO_ALG_FIPS_UNAPPROVED)
 
 /*
  * Given the type and mask that specify the flags restrictions on a template
--- a/include/linux/crypto.h
+++ b/include/linux/crypto.h
@@ -125,6 +125,18 @@
 #define CRYPTO_ALG_FIPS_INTERNAL	0x00020000
 
 /*
+ * Mark an algorithm as unapproved by FIPS.
+ *
+ * Downstream flag introduced to meet the FIPS certification
+ * requirements for crypto_alg implementations that aren't intended
+ * for cryptographic uses, but still exposed through the crypto API.
+ *
+ * Gets propagated from spawns up to relying crypto_instance's, as per
+ * being a member of CRYPTO_ALG_INHERITED_FLAGS.
+ */
+#define CRYPTO_ALG_FIPS_UNAPPROVED	0x40000000
+
+/*
  * Transform masks and values (for crt_flags).
  */
 #define CRYPTO_TFM_NEED_KEY		0x00000001
